// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_CRYPTO_PBKDF2_LENGTH
// RUNTIME: exercise via `anubis run` (this is a runtime panic; `anubis check` still passes,
// this is a *runtime* fail-closed gate).
// Companion of pbkdf2_hmac_sha256_zero_length_should_fail_closed.anb: negative dkLen was
// silently coerced to 0 by `.max(0)` — now honestly reported so a signed-overflow at the
// call site is caught rather than laundered.
fn main() {
    print(pbkdf2_hmac_sha256("password", "salt", 100, -1));
}
